      <activity id="13b6d2dd-4515-5dfc-bddb-93d2ef6eb05d" activityNameId="275615a8-2bbd-5a0d-83eb-20a729dd5f41" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Yarn production, bast fibres</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Yarn production, bast fibres
Inventory refers to the processing of 1 kg fibres only, without the production of the fibres itself.;
UUID: 10004d2b-e7b0-3584-b73f-69a240182122
The inventories include energy consumption, transport and infrastructure related to the processing of bast fibres to yarn (opening, batching, cardening, spinning).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Opening, batching, cardening, combing and spinning are the main processes of the yarn production. Mechanical cleaning and no chemical cleaning was assumed for this study. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume:  
Sampling: Data are from expert interviews and literature.  
Extrapolations: Infrastructure of mechanical processings of fibres was assumed similar to packaging plant
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_10004d2b-e7b0-3584-b73f-69a240182122.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="54f55fae-bf70-52c2-b2bc-7b92fd55ae8e" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
